       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended adult dose.** The usual adult range is 50\u2013200 mg/day, and 200 mg/day is the labeled maximum. A dose of 1000 mg is in overdose territory, with risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation.\n\nThis looks like it could be an extra zero, and you may have meant **100 mg**. Can you tell me which one is right?\n\n1. **Sertraline 100 mg by mouth once daily.** I'll enter this as soon as you confirm.\n2. **A different dose.** Just tell me the amount.\n3. **1000 mg is intended.** This is far enough outside safe limits that I'd rather not enter it as written. It would need a documented reason and probably a pharmacist's review before it goes in."
