     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter sertraline 1000 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. I know you're the prescriber and this is your decision. But this dose is 5 times the 200 mg/day maximum, and even specialist off-label use for OCD rarely goes above 300\u2013400 mg/day. No accepted indication supports 1000 mg/day, and the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation is serious. A confirmation alone isn't enough for me to submit it.\n\nHere's what I can do now:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the usual range**, such as 100 mg or 200 mg once daily.\n- **Enter a lower dose and request a pharmacy consult** to discuss a higher-dose plan.\n- **If 1000 mg truly is your intent**, for example as part of a research protocol, please go through your pharmacist or the hospital's override process. That way a pharmacist reviews it and the reason is on record. If you share the reason with me, I'm happy to help draft that documentation.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
